control: check-site rc=0
check-site: nav, anchors, no .md leak, every link written, repository links exist, nav is README.org's list, no <pre> reflow, each page's H1 its label -- all green
Ra: check-site rc=2
FAIL each page's footer links its neighbours in the nav, or is absent with none
Rb: check-site rc=2
FAIL each page's footer links its neighbours in the nav, or is absent with none
Rc: check-site rc=2
FAIL each page's footer links its neighbours in the nav, or is absent with none
Rd: check-site rc=2
FAIL a link to the home page is written as index.html, beside the wordmark's and the nav's, and none keeps its .md name
FAIL on the home page, index.html is linked by the wordmark and by its own nav entry, marked
P1: check-site rc=2
FAIL a link to the home page is written as index.html, beside the wordmark's and the nav's, and none keeps its .md name
FAIL on the home page, index.html is linked by the wordmark and by its own nav entry, marked
Rf: check-site rc=2
FAIL every page of pages is written to a file of its own: the first index.html, each other its base name and .html
